            <ArticleTitle>[Muscle necroses--CT aspects].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>190-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In four patients muscle necroses were observed. In two patients these were caused by intraoperative positioning, in one by having worked with a pneumatic hammer and in one possibly by alcohol. CT showed hypodense areas in the affected muscles which were--in the state of subacute necroses--surrounded by hyperaemic borders. The diagnosis was confirmed by puncture or biopsy. After six months hypodense areas were still perceptible in the atrophic muscles of two patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
